{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789859485,"nonce":"OWP/oW+kOknSGDeR4ncxQ2nXIvs=","message":"Done in ee94a90a, together with 2a51f66 — the lock is meaningless without the re-read and the re-read is unsafe without the lock.\n\nThe open-time pid lock is gone entirely: readers take nothing, so an open termui no longer blocks agents. Writers take an advisory flock on .git/git-work/write.lock for one read-modify-commit. Using a kernel lock rather than a pid file means there is no stale-lock cleanup at all — the kernel releases it when the process dies, SIGKILL included.","files":null}]}